Each item reduces to a set of league-rule facts about the outcomes, so I worked through them one at a time. A few readings I applied consistently:

- A label of No negates the question, so "Will X avoid Y?" with No means X does Y.
- "Top N points" means at least N+1. "Hit the N-point mark" means at least N.
- "Pot-one", "seed", "protected slot" and "not unseeded" all mean seeded. "Unprotected" and "denied pot-one" mean not seeded.
- "Lose the final" or "runner-up" means the second-place finisher. Exactly two teams qualify, and the Cup winner and runner-up are those two.
- For the group items, I checked whether each pair or set of outcomes can be jointly true or jointly false under the rules, and I built a consistent league state for each bound I claimed.
- For H394 the six outcomes are "team X qualifies", and exactly two teams qualify, so the count is exactly 2. Both at_least_k and at_most_k fit, and I chose at_most_k.
- For H387 Gorton being seed implies Gorton has at least one point, so the chain is outcome 2 then outcome 1.

